WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.708 --> 00:00:03.625
(orchestral music)

00:00:14.377 --> 00:00:15.413
- Yeah, there's no room for fear

00:00:15.413 --> 00:00:17.246
in this world of mine.

00:00:18.217 --> 00:00:19.217
Forget that.

00:00:27.138 --> 00:00:28.684
Has been a bit of a road.

00:00:28.684 --> 00:00:30.272
I first saw wingwalking

00:00:30.272 --> 00:00:33.517
when I was kinda in my early twenties.

00:00:33.517 --> 00:00:34.957
I was bumping around and I didn't want

00:00:34.957 --> 00:00:36.234
to go to college.

00:00:36.234 --> 00:00:38.766
I didn't know what I wanted to do in life.

00:00:38.766 --> 00:00:40.786
Saw an advert for my local airshow

00:00:40.786 --> 00:00:42.864
and saw a nanosecond of a wingwalker go by

00:00:42.864 --> 00:00:44.364
in a Javelin and that was it.

00:00:44.364 --> 00:00:45.535
I was owned.

00:00:45.535 --> 00:00:46.955
I decided right then and there that

00:00:46.955 --> 00:00:49.575
that was going to be the rest of my life.

00:00:49.575 --> 00:00:51.870
It took me from that point seven years

00:00:51.870 --> 00:00:53.022
of begging and pleading every

00:00:53.022 --> 00:00:55.040
wingwalking team in North America,

00:00:55.040 --> 00:00:58.198
to basically just even
get me up in the sky.

00:00:58.198 --> 00:01:01.115
(orchestral music)

00:01:15.819 --> 00:01:18.061
It's like being in a
category five hurricane

00:01:18.061 --> 00:01:20.919
on a roller coaster from
hell with no way off.

00:01:20.919 --> 00:01:22.772
(laughs)

00:01:22.772 --> 00:01:24.455
- [Interviewer] So why
do you keep doing it?

00:01:24.455 --> 00:01:25.944
- [Carol] Because I'm a mad woman.

00:01:25.944 --> 00:01:26.936
(laughs)

00:01:26.936 --> 00:01:29.853
(orchestral music)

00:02:08.625 --> 00:02:11.367
The airplane that you
see behind me right now,

00:02:11.367 --> 00:02:12.579
in a weird twist of fate

00:02:12.579 --> 00:02:13.997
that's actually the very first airplane

00:02:13.997 --> 00:02:17.283
that I ever wingwalked on
and now it's my airplane.

00:02:17.283 --> 00:02:18.394
My life just wouldn't be worth it

00:02:18.394 --> 00:02:19.628
if I couldn't wake up in the morning

00:02:19.628 --> 00:02:21.127
and go do this.

00:02:21.127 --> 00:02:22.421
C'mon.

00:02:22.421 --> 00:02:26.088
Doesn't it look like
the funnest thing ever?

00:02:27.919 --> 00:02:31.345
That's the reason I get
out of bed in the morning.

00:02:31.345 --> 00:02:32.427
That's what makes me smile.

00:02:32.427 --> 00:02:33.892
That's what makes me not care

00:02:33.892 --> 00:02:35.508
if I have to work 16 hours straight

00:02:35.508 --> 00:02:37.311
for five days in a row if I get to go

00:02:37.311 --> 00:02:39.728
and do this at the end of it.

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:47.808
Anytime that you can aspire

00:02:47.808 --> 00:02:52.208
to see a human, another human being

00:02:52.731 --> 00:02:55.619
kind of achieve their inner thing

00:02:55.619 --> 00:02:58.956
and that when you can witness
triumph over adversity,

00:02:58.956 --> 00:03:00.744
I mean it just kind of motivates you

00:03:00.744 --> 00:03:03.338
to fuckin' be proud of your race.

00:03:03.338 --> 00:03:04.869
It's like when you see those great videos

00:03:04.869 --> 00:03:06.882
of dogs doing super cools things,

00:03:06.882 --> 00:03:09.918
doesn't that just make you love dogs?

00:03:09.918 --> 00:03:10.751
Same thing.

00:03:10.751 --> 00:03:12.133
(laughs)

00:03:12.133 --> 00:03:15.050
(orchestral music)

